{
  "source": {
    "package": "@oh-my-pi/pi-catalog",
    "version": "18.13.3",
    "extracted": "2026-10-30",
    "upstream": [
      "packages/catalog/src/compat/rules.json — `providers.<id>` seed rows (model ids, api, baseUrl) and `auth.providers` (login kind, display name, env keys)",
      "packages/catalog/src/compat/rules/providers/<id>.kdl — authored provider contract (discovery label, seed api/base-url, default model)",
      "packages/catalog/src/compat/rules/runtime/behavior.kdl — `api-routes` (per-model protocol routes; a mixed-protocol provider needs one record per protocol)",
      "packages/catalog/src/provider-models/*.ts — factory default base URLs for providers that author no seed row"
    ],
    "rules": [
      "One record per omp API-key LLM provider that the models.dev snapshot lacks. Not materialized: ids already in the catalog, naming aliases of a catalog row, non-model providers (search / local-inference / no env key), and OAuth- or device-code-only logins.",
      "`api` is the provider's materializable protocol (anthropic-messages / openai-completions / openai-responses / typesafe). A mixed-protocol provider gets one record per protocol — a custom-provider declaration carries exactly one `api`.",
      "`baseUrl` is the provider's authored seed base URL or factory default; null when omp ships none, or when omp's default is a loopback http:// endpoint (the declaration store requires https), so the operator supplies it at save time.",
      "`models` are the provider's seed model ids (or its default model when it ships no seed rows), capped at 20; empty when omp carries neither.",
      "A mixed-protocol provider contributes one record per protocol; `sourceProviderId` names the omp provider where a record id differs from it."
    ]
  },
